From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Charkov <alchark@flipper.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:47:15 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: Set gpioN aliases on RK3576

With no alias, the OS is free to number the GPIO chips arbitrarily, such
as in probe order, which is what Linux kernel's rockchip_gpio_probe() does
if its of_alias_get_id(np, "gpio") fails.

This results in GPIO chip numbers arbitrarily shuffled in userspace,
causing confusion and pain.

Set gpioN aliases in the SoC .dtsi, just like other SoC versions do.

Signed-off-by: Alexey Charkov <alchark@flipper.net>
---
Alexey Charkov's "arm64: dts: rockchip: Set gpioN aliases on RK3576" v1,
posted 2026-09-14, under review on linux-rockchip as of 2026-09-14:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260914-rk3576-gpio-aliases-v1-1-ce5f86f9ae0e@flipper.net/

Regenerated against this series' base, v7.2.5 plus 100-102; the change is
identical to the posting.

 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
index 353a86746..7c34f8aab 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576.dtsi
@@ -21,6 +21,11 @@ / {
 	#size-cells = <2>;
 
 	aliases {
+		gpio0 = &gpio0;
+		gpio1 = &gpio1;
+		gpio2 = &gpio2;
+		gpio3 = &gpio3;
+		gpio4 = &gpio4;
 		i2c0 = &i2c0;
 		i2c1 = &i2c1;
 		i2c2 = &i2c2;
-- 
2.43.0

